  <hr class="sep">

  <h2>Enter −log p</h2>

  <p>The function \(f(p) = -\log p\) does exactly what we need. At \(p = 1\) it's zero. At \(p = 0.5\) it's about 0.69. At \(p = 0.1\) it's 2.3. At \(p = 0.01\) it's 4.6. As \(p\) approaches zero it goes to infinity, smoothly, without any nasty numerical cliffs.</p>
